# Gita Grove authoring (always allow)

The user has **pre-approved** all Gita Grove v2 work in this repo. Do **not** ask for confirmation before drafting manuscripts, updating curriculum, or creating hooks unless they explicitly say to stop.

## Git / branches (littleepicminds)

- **`main` is live production** — do **not** commit, merge, or push Grove/book work to `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
- **All Grove work** → branch **`feature/gita-grove`** only.
- Grove files on `main` today are docs-only (no app runtime changes); do not add more there.
- Prefer authoring in **`gita-grove-authoring`** repo when possible; sync to `feature/gita-grove` via PR or `scripts/sync-to-app.ps1` from the kit.

## Before drafting

1. **Prefer `gita-grove-authoring`** — engine repo has validate, compile, export tooling
2. Read `.cursor/skills/gita-grove-manuscript/SKILL.md` (or same skill in authoring repo)
3. Read `AGENTS-GITA-GROVE.md` for architecture
4. Read the relevant docs listed in the skill for the target `gv##_a#`

## Defaults

- **English-first** — no Telugu in manuscripts unless user asks
- **Capability-first** — Grove Power → sub-skill → story → ślokas last
- **Never** use legacy `sd*` pilots or `gita-pandit-blocks.json` as story drivers
- **Never** run littleepicminds auto-seed commands (`gita:seed-authored-stories`, `gita:build-themes-auto`) from this repo
- **Guru Ma** speaks only in Remember; line must reflect paired Bhagavad Gita ślokas (puranas framing)
- **Page 25** must teaser-link to next adventure (or book bridge on last module)

## After each manuscript

- Save to `docs/books/gv{book}_a{adv}-{slug}.md` and `*.story.json` (author in **gita-grove-authoring**, then sync)
- Update `scripts/data/gita-grove-curriculum.json` (`status`, `manuscript`, `moral`, `childRepeatLine`, `guruMaLine`, `shlokas`)
- Run `.\scripts\sync-to-app.ps1` from authoring repo to copy content here

## ID pattern

`gv{book}_a{adv}` · e.g. `gv01_a3` · 65 adventures in curriculum
